# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Lets the person at the computer open a Google phone in fastboot mode (the
# installer app, or a Chromium-based browser for the web flasher) without root.
#
# systemd 262's own 70-uaccess.rules already does this for every device with a
# fastboot interface (ID_DEBUG_APPLIANCE=android, then TAG+="uaccess"), so on a
# current Arch or Omarchy this file changes nothing. It is for distributions
# whose systemd doesn't carry that rule yet. Untested in this spike.
#
# Matches the interface, not a product ID: vendor class 0xff, subclass 0x42,
# protocol 0x03 is fastboot (AOSP system/core/fastboot/fastboot.cpp). Sorted
# after 50-udev-default.rules (which sets ID_USB_INTERFACES) and before
# 73-seat-late.rules (which turns the uaccess tag into an ACL).
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="18d1", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACES}=="*:ff4203:*", TAG+="uaccess"
